Chimera's fix to the fork's Bink 2 decoder (wasm/bink/build.sh applies it).

Block flags: a run of flags read from the file was added to the count without
checking it against how many flags are left, so a bad run wrote past the end
of the row or column flag array (found by AddressSanitizer, on damaged copies
of the Remastered Collection's movies). The run is capped at what's left; a
real file's run always fits, so nothing it decodes changes.

--- a/libavcodec/bink2.c
+++ b/libavcodec/bink2.c
@@ -214,9 +214,11 @@
             flags_left -= nb_coded;
             if (flags_left > 0) {
                 temp = get_bits(gb, bits);
+                mode = temp == (1 << bits) - 1U ? 1 : 3;
+                /* A run past the flags there are would write past the array. */
+                temp = FFMIN(temp, flags_left);
                 flags_left -= temp;
                 nb_coded += temp;
-                mode = temp == (1 << bits) - 1U ? 1 : 3;
             }
 
             temp = (flag << 0x1f) >> 0x1f & 0xff;
